  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "USE OF PROCEEDS The shares of our common stock offered pursuant to this prospectus supplement and the accompanying prospectus include newly issued shares\nthat may be offered and sold by us to or through the sales agents, acting as our sales agents or as principals, and borrowed shares of\nour common stock that may be offered and sold by the forward purchasers through the forward sellers, acting as agents for the forward\npurchasers. We intend to contribute any net proceeds we receive from this offering to the Operating Partnership in exchange for OP Units.\nThe Operating Partnership may use the net proceeds contributed by us for general corporate and working capital purposes, which may include\nproperty acquisitions, commercial loan and investment opportunities and repayment of debt, including amounts outstanding under the Credit\nAgreement. The Revolver has a termination date of February 4, ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "RISK FACTORS Investing in our common stock involves risks. In addition to other information in this prospectus supplement, you should carefully\nconsider the risks described in our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025 and subsequent Annual Reports\non Form 10-K and Quarterly Reports on Form 10-Q under \u201cItem 1A. Risk Factors,\u201d as well as other information and data set\nforth in this prospectus supplement, the accompanying prospectus and the documents incorporated by reference herein and therein before\nmaking an investment decision with respect to our common stock. The occurrence of any of the following risks could materially and adversely\naffect our business, prospects, financial condition, results of operations and our ability to make cash distributions to our stockholders,\nwhich could cause you to lose all or a part of your investment in our common stock. ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
